# Backend-only credentials. Never put them in Vite/frontend .env files.
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM Provider — Google Gemini (recommended: free, no card, generous tier)
#   Get key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Advocate Agent configuration (for the multi-advocate pipeline)
# Mode: "mock" or "real"
#   mock  - deterministic, offline, no credentials. Output is derived from
#           the trusted case context, so it stays realistic & reproducible.
#           This is the safe default.
#   real  - calls an external model. Requires AGENT_PROVIDER, AGENT_MODEL,
#           AGENT_API_KEY, and AGENT_BASE_URL (except for tencent_tokenhub,
#           which has a documented default).
#
# AGENT_MODE=real NEVER falls back to mock. If the provider fails, the
# affected advocate reports FAILED and the deterministic analysis is
# unaffected. It never presents canned output as a live model response.
#
# This file is the committed template. Copy it to `.env` for local settings;
# `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENT_MODE=mock
AGENT_PROVIDER=mock
AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=20
AGENT_TEMPERATURE=0.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL OLLAMA — offline, no cloud API, no real credential
#
# Ollama serves an OpenAI-compatible API, so it reuses the existing
# openai_compatible provider. No Ollama-specific provider code is required.
#
# AGENT_API_KEY is a throwaway placeholder: Ollama does not authenticate on
# localhost, but the provider requires a non-empty key by contract.
#
# CONTEXT LENGTH IS THE TRAP. Ollama gives every model a 4096-token context by
# default. The advocate prompt alone is ~4000 tokens (system rules + side prompt
# + output schema + case context), so at 4096 Ollama silently drops roughly half
# the prompt and leaves no room for the answer. The run then fails with
# OUTPUT_TRUNCATED and no obvious cause.
#
# Fix it one of two ways:
#   a) raise the server default and restart Ollama, then use the plain model:
#          OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=16384
#   b) derive a variant that bakes in a larger context (no restart needed):
#          FROM qwen3:8b
#          PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
#          ollama create qwen3-ctx16k -f Modelfile
#
# MODEL SIZE MATTERS MORE THAN PARAMETER COUNT HERE. An 18 GB model on an 8 GB
# GPU runs mostly on CPU (qwen3.8:27b measured ~5 tokens/second). qwen3:8b is
# ~5.2 GB and stays 100% on the GPU, which is dramatically faster.
#
# AGENT_MAX_TOKENS may need raising. Thinking models count their reasoning
# toward the completion budget, so a limit that suits a cloud model can cut the
# JSON off mid-string. The provider reports that case as OUTPUT_TRUNCATED rather
# than as malformed JSON.
#
# Verify before use:
#   curl http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1/models
#   python -m app.agents.providers.diagnostics --list
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_MODE=real
# AGENT_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# AGENT_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
# AGENT_MODEL=qwen3-ctx16k:latest
# AGENT_API_KEY=ollama
# AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900
# AGENT_TEMPERATURE=0
# AGENT_MAX_TOKENS=8192

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tencent TokenHub (Singapore region)
#   OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions. The base URL below is the default, so
#   AGENT_BASE_URL may be omitted for this provider.
#
#   AGENT_MODEL is intentionally NOT pinned here. The model is a deployment
#   choice and is benchmarked in Stage 4C. Any model available to the account
#   can be used, for example:
#       hy4-preview | deepseek/deepseek-flash | glm-5.3-flash | glm-5.3 | kimi-k3
#   Not every account has every model — verify before a live run:
#       python -m app.agents.providers.diagnostics --list
#
#   AGENT_API_KEY is the authoritative setting. As a documented convenience,
#   TENCENT_TOKENHUB_API_KEY is accepted as a fallback for this provider only.
#   The value is never logged, never returned by /api/health, and never sent
#   to the browser. Never commit a real key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_MODE=real
# AGENT_PROVIDER=tencent_tokenhub
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://tokenhub-intl.tencentmaas.com/v1
# AGENT_MODEL=
# AGENT_API_KEY=
# TENCENT_TOKENHUB_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Gemini Developer API — Stage 4 advocates (current active provider)
#
#   Gemini exposes an official OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so this reuses the
#   existing openai_compatible provider. No Gemini-specific provider code
#   exists, and none is needed.
#
#   AGENT_API_KEY is the credential for the advocates. It is deliberately NOT
#   the GEMINI_API_KEY above: that one belongs to the intake pipeline
#   (app/llm/gemini_client.py). The two systems use the same underlying service
#   but stay architecturally separate, so configuring one never silently
#   switches the other to live calls.
#
#   AGENT_MODEL: gemini-3.8-flash is what this project was asked to target.
#   Note the intake client defaults to gemini-3.6-flash. Model availability is
#   per-account and changes over time, so confirm the ID your key can actually
#   reach before a live run:
#       python -m app.agents.providers.diagnostics --list
#
#   AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS is 60 because this is a cloud API, not a local model.
#   AGENT_MAX_TOKENS is raised above the 2000 default because Gemini 3.x Flash
#   is a thinking model: thinking tokens count toward the completion budget, and
#   too low a cap cuts the JSON off mid-string. The provider reports that as
#   OUTPUT_TRUNCATED rather than as malformed JSON.
#
#   AGENT_REASONING_EFFORT is OPTIONAL and unset by default, so the outbound
#   request body is unchanged unless you ask for it. Set it to "low" to request
#   lighter hidden reasoning. The hint travels as an optional provider-specific
#   request field and never becomes part of the generic provider contract.
#
#   AGENT_MAX_RETRIES defaults to 0 (no retry). Gemini returns a transient
#   HTTP 503 UNAVAILABLE under load ("This model is currently experiencing high
#   demand"), which fails an advocate through no fault of the request. The
#   provider already classifies 503 as retryable; setting this to 2 makes that
#   machinery reachable. Auth failures are never retried, whatever this is set to.
#
#   The credential is never logged, never returned by /api/health, and never
#   sent to the browser. Never commit a real key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AGENT_MODE=real
# AGENT_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# AGENT_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# AGENT_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# AGENT_API_KEY=
# AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# AGENT_TEMPERATURE=0
# AGENT_MAX_TOKENS=8192
# AGENT_MAX_RETRIES=2
# AGENT_REASONING_EFFORT=

# Alternative providers (uncomment to use)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# TENCENT_MODEL=hunyuan-turbos-latest
